The paper’s main theorem is constructive rather than a hardness result, so “output a bent polynomial” would be a lookup task and is not acceptable. I’m checking whether a related witness search—such as preimage finding for its vectorial cubic map—survives the paper’s coordinate formulas and obvious algebraic inversion attacks.
